Language English

Book Hall2 Ordered No Keep Looped

	// Hall2 can be explored from Hall1, the Foyer, or the Study

	Page PlaceHall2ViaHall1
		Triggered By @ExploreHall2ViaHall1
		
		Add TileHall2, TokenWallHall2!

		Text """
			Feeble light oozes from the {c:TileGallery} door into the hallway. 
			You can see now that the hallway continues into the dark. Place the
			{c:TileHall2} tile and a wall as indicated.
		"""
		
		exploredHall2ViaHall1 = true
		exploredHall2 = true
	End Page PlaceHall2ViaHall1
	
	Page PlacePart2
		Add TokenExploreFoyerViaHall2, TokenExploreStudyViaHall2
		
		Text """
			Doors off the hall lead deeper into the house. Place Explore tokens
			as indicated.
		"""
	End Page PlacePart2
	
	Page PlaceInvestigator
		Visible When exploredBackyardNicely
		Add TokenHall2Investigators
		
		Text """
			Neither {c:EventChosenInvestigator} nor the investigator who is
			Exploring walks down the hall, but any one of the others may move 1
			space into {c:TileHall2} as indicated.
		"""
		
		Remove TokenHall2Investigators
	End Page PlaceInvestigator
	
	Page PlaceHall2Evidence
		Add TokenSearchHall2Evidence
		
		Text """
			A table has been knocked over, scattering its contents across the
			room. <i>That broken lamp on the floor might help navigate this 
			room,</i> you think to yourself. Place a Search token as indicated.
		"""
		
		Exit
	End Page PlaceHall2Evidence

	Page SearchEvidence
		Triggered By @SearchHall2Evidence
		
		Prolog "The upended table has spilled its contents across the floor."
		Button "Search"
		
		Remove TokenSearchHall2Evidence
		
		Text QItemEvidenceHall2 """
			You start with the lamp but it is too broken to use. Besides the
			lamp, there is a dead plant and scraps of paper tossed around. One
			of the scraps catches your eye:  it is spattered in dried blood.
			The note talks about preparations for a ritual and mentions
			something about a chapel and crypt. The
			author of the note wants to stop the ritual and it is clear he will
			do anything to stop it. The note is signed <<Henry Smythe.>>

			Gain the {c:QItemEvidenceHall2} Unique Item, then discard this
			Search token.
		"""

		Exit
	End Page SearchEvidence

End Book Hall2